From 1c991c049cd1e197af31ab2c817c1ded71d855f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:14:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/30] Add Bilibili QR login and session core to LiveHime
 plugin

plugins/livehime/core is a Swift package (unit-tested with `swift test`)
compiled into the plugin: v0.1.2's identity and live-room clients, plus a
QR login client, a versioned Keychain credential store that recognizes
v0.1.2 items and migrates their WebKit cookies, and a SessionCoordinator.
The coordinator only reports "ready" after identity and room load, and
only returns to "signed out" when Bilibili rejects the login; network or
API errors stay in "failed" with the login kept and a retry offered.

The dock gains an account section driven by the core's state through a
small C interface. The automation vendor adds GetAccountState,
StartQRLogin and CancelQRLogin; LIVEHIME_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE lets tests use
an isolated Keychain item.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
